// wholesale pack -- projections (epic memql#5533, issue memql#5555).
//
// A CONCEPT FIELD IS NOT A READABLE FIELD. A query with no shape answers
// the graph bundle, whose payload fields sit one level down -- so a caller
// reading `row.companyName` off it gets "" and no error, which is the
// failure mode this file exists to remove. Every read in this pack names a
// shape.
//
// THERE IS NO PUBLIC PROJECTION OF AN APPLICATION, and the absence is a
// decision rather than an omission. reviewspack ships two projections of
// its review because one of them is served to an unauthenticated browser;
// nothing in THIS pack ever is. An application is a named person's business
// contact details against a named company, and the pack declares a shopper
// FORM with no matching shopper READ -- a shopper may submit one and may
// not read one back, not even their own. Reading their own would need the
// verified Shopify customer principal that issue memql#5550 recorded as the
// answer for a buyer's own data and deliberately did not build; when a
// client needs it, it is an addition here rather than a rewrite, because
// reach is declared per route.

use wholesale.concepts.{ application, applicationDecision, entitlement, wholesaleSettings, documentVersion }
use wholesale.concepts.{ privateLink, acceptance, emailSend }
use shopify.overlay.concepts.{ store }

// THE PACK'S ONE CROSS-DOMAIN READ, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY THREE FIELDS.
//
// An adapter has to know what the bound store can do -- native B2B is
// available below Plus since 2026-04-02, but with at most three catalogs
// (the connector record, 1.3), and an adapter that discovered that ceiling
// at the fourth grant would discover it in a merchant's live store.
//
// shopify.overlay ALREADY SHIPS storeFull and this does not use it. That
// shape projects adminTokenRef, storefrontTokenRef and webhookSecretRef,
// and epic memql#5530's D10 settled what holding those is worth: "a
// credential reference the serving path was never handed cannot reach a
// response header, a served document or a log line". The same reasoning
// applies one tier up. This pack never needs a credential reference, so it
// declares a projection that cannot carry one -- the omission is the
// safety property rather than an economy.
//
// The store row is readable by a cluster owner or a developer only
// (@rowAuthz(clusterOwner, rankFloor="developer")), so this read ANSWERING
// NOTHING is the ordinary case for a merchant rather than a fault. entitlement.go's storePlan treats it as
// such, and each adapter says for itself what an unknown plan means for it.
@description("What this pack needs to know about a bound store: which plan it is on and whether it is a development store. NOT its credentials -- storeFull projects three token references and this projection exists so the wholesale pack can never hold one.")
@row
shape store wholesaleStorePlan {
  row.id
  plan
  isDevelopment
}

@description("An application as its MERCHANT sees it, whole. The only projection of this concept, because the only reader is the merchant it was addressed to.")
@row
shape application applicationFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  siteId
  companyName
  applicantName
  applicantEmail
  accountId
  source
  addedBy
  submittedAt
  row.createdAt
}

@description("A decision, whole. Append-only, so a row is a decision and this is all of it.")
@row
shape applicationDecision applicationDecisionFull {
  row.id
  applicationId
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  transition
  decidedBy
  principalKind
  note
  accountId
  decidedAt
  row.createdAt
}

@description("An entitlement, whole. row.createdAt is the version clock: the time of the newest version, which any write of the row moves. When the attempt was made, when trade prices went on and when they came off are attemptedAt, grantedAt and revokedAt.")
@row
shape entitlement entitlementFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  applicationId
  storeId
  buyerEmail
  adapter
  state
  reference
  error
  errorCode
  shopifyCustomerId
  customerCreated
  accountId
  direction
  attempt
  attemptedAt
  grantedAt
  revokedAt
  row.createdAt
}

@description("One store's wholesale settings.")
@row
shape wholesaleSettings wholesaleSettingsFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  applicationsOpen
  entitlementAdapter
  introText
  accountId
  siteId
  staffEmail
  termsRequired
  linkLifetimeDays
  acceptanceText
  senderIdentityId
  termsTemplateId
  approvedTemplateId
  rejectedTemplateId
  revokedTemplateId
  row.createdAt
}

@description("A document version, whole: its body and the fingerprint of it. Append-only, so a row is a version and this is all of it.")
@row
shape documentVersion documentVersionFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  accountId
  kind
  label
  body
  sha256
  publishedBy
  publishedAt
  row.createdAt
}

@description("A document version WITHOUT its body: what tells whether a kind has a version, which is the newest, and what a history lists. The reads that run on every settings read and every shopper submission to a store that requires its terms read through this, and never carry a body of up to 200 KB they do not show.")
@row
shape documentVersion wholesaleDocumentVersionBrief {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  accountId
  kind
  label
  sha256
  publishedBy
  publishedAt
  row.createdAt
}

@description("A private link, whole, its token hash included. NO READ PROJECTS IT: the token lookup and the application's link read both project privateLinkPublic, so a token hash leaves no read. The whole row, as a reader of the concept would name it.")
@row
shape privateLink privateLinkFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  accountId
  siteId
  applicationId
  purpose
  tokenHash
  issuedAt
  expiresAt
  usedAt
  row.createdAt
}

@description("A private link WITHOUT its token hash: what the token lookup answers, so the read that a shopper's token reaches never carries a hash back.")
@row
shape privateLink privateLinkPublic {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  accountId
  siteId
  applicationId
  purpose
  issuedAt
  expiresAt
  usedAt
  row.createdAt
}

@description("An acceptance, whole: its evidence and the versions it names. Written once, so a row is an acceptance and this is all of it.")
@row
shape acceptance acceptanceFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  accountId
  applicationId
  applicantEmail
  signedName
  acceptedAt
  termsVersionId
  termsSha256
  mapVersionId
  mapSha256
  statement
  clientAddress
  userAgent
  linkIssuedAt
  row.createdAt
}

@description("An email's record, whole: which email, which attempt, the lane's request id and what came of it. It carries no address, no field of the message and no token, because the row holds none.")
@row
shape emailSend emailSendFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  storeId
  accountId
  applicationId
  kind
  attempt
  requestId
  templateId
  state
  reason
  sentAt
  requestedBy
  row.createdAt
}

// ---- the store statistics walk (the 2026-11-11 store statistics design) ----
//
// What the walk reads of this pack: which buyers a store granted, and which
// stores have wholesale set up. The row's store id and nothing the figures do
// not use -- no owner, no adapter, no reference and no account.

@description("An entitlement as the store statistics walk reads it: the store, the buyer it was granted to and its state, so the walk can tell a wholesale order from a retail one.")
@row
shape entitlement entitlementStatisticsRef {
  row.id
  storeId
  buyerEmail
  state
}

@description("One store's wholesale settings as the store statistics walk reads them: only that the store has them.")
@row
shape wholesaleSettings wholesaleSettingsStatisticsRef {
  row.id
  storeId
}
